 "about": "The shared cases of the need of a drain. The app replays them in Swift, the pipeline in Python and the backend in SQL, so the three tellings of the rule cannot drift apart. The cases were written by hand from the rules in app/InfrastructureGO/Resources/spawn_rules.json. Each tier case gives the instant of the question, the last look at the drain by anyone, the last look by the player who asks, and whether a storm window is open. The tier is the need of the drain, which decides its crate and the points of a look. Who lives at a drain is decided by rules that are still being tuned and are tested in Swift alone until they have settled.",
